Create a Java program to manage employees and their departments.
Define an Employee class with attributes:
•	id
•	name
•	salary
•	deptName
•	organization
Create 10 employees belonging to at least 3 departments.
Implement operations to:
1.	Calculate the average salary of employees in each department.
2.	Sort employees by name.
3.	Find the top 3 highest-paid employees.
4.	Display employees earning ≥ 50,000 in each department.
Instructions
1.	Create a class named Employee with private fields and public getters/setters.
2.	Create a class named EmployeeManagement with a main() method.
3.	Use a List<Employee> (e.g., ArrayList<Employee>) to store employees.
4.	Use Java Streams or Collections utilities to perform filtering, sorting, and grouping.
5.	Print results in a clear, tabular format.
Requirements
•	Use Core Java only (no frameworks).
•	Use Java 8 or higher for Stream API.
•	Code should be modular and readable.
•	Show clear console output for all 4 tasks.
